AUDIO: 'Hello everyone, welcome back to the channel. With you Ollie from "The Road With Love." We just finished building what we believe is the perfect camper van for autonomous travel . I did a lot of research before starting. I made sure to use the best materials I'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'could find for this van. So if you\'re planning to convert your van, want to hire someone to do it, or are just curious—this video is for you. If you want to get straight to the point, I\'ll leave a link to a downloadable file with everything'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we used for our build. You can view it at any time. However, I highly recommend watching this video to the end to understand why we made such informed decisions about the choice of materials.'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Let\'s start with the basic building material—it\'s 16.5- millimeter, it seems, laminated plywood. Since it is already laminated, it is much easier to get a nice finished result.'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You don\'t need to worry about finishing it, at least on the outside . It is always important to varnish or finish the edges, but we used this material where it would be too difficult to apply aluminum . Okay, next we have this'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wonderful material that we used for the ceiling. It\'s from a company called Deco Plus. In fact, these are PVC panels with imitation lining . The advantages of using this'

[01:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'material over wood siding are that it is much lighter and does not require painting or the care associated with wood. They connect very conveniently. They have special holes through which they'

[01:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can be attached. Apply adhesive to the back, then simply slide panel after panel—and you have a beautiful wall or ceiling. Although they look quite stiff, they are'

[01:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'surprisingly flexible. We used them in the front of our van and they proved flexible enough to curve around the bed; Honestly, I don\'t even know what we would do without them'

[01:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '. So, if you are looking for an option for beautiful walls and ceilings, choose this one. I want to add: another of our favorite materials is the one we feel but don\'t see. This is our'

[02:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'isolation. We chose a cork-based spray-on insulation called Corkon. So, we did this because we had such a large area, some of which was already insulated and some of which was not, and we'

[02:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'decided to start with a clean slate and cover every possible surface with it. Some of the benefits of using Corkon are its antimicrobial, antibacterial properties, and in my opinion , it repels water well. It\'s'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'easy to apply after a little preparation , and, yes, it works very well. Next is the aluminum composite panel. This is actually from Bunnings. You can buy such a'

[02:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'panel with a black or white back . You can also buy them at sign shops. It\'s a little bit of aluminum, a very, very thin layer of aluminum, then some kind of composite'

[02:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'material, and another layer of aluminum on top. The result is a very stiff, strong and lightweight panel. We used them'

[03:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'during assembly as the bottom for our cabinets. I\'ll show you how it fits perfectly into our aluminum T- slot, and we\'ve also used it in a few places where we needed an'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'extra lightweight panel that wasn\'t wood and wouldn\'t deteriorate over time . So, yes, aluminum composite panel. Keep it in mind when you need a nice thin board. They come in huge sizes, are'

[03:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'extremely strong and durable. That\'s all. Okay, let\'s move on to our aesthetic part. This is a flexible wooden slat panel. There are many companies that make them. It\'s a wood veneer'

[03:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'glued onto paper or something similar. I do n\'t know exactly how they do it, but traditionally, to make a panel like this, you would have to cut all these slats , paint'

[03:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'each one individually, and then painstakingly attach them to a board, wall, or something else. This is a lot of unnecessary hassle. You pay extra for everything to be already done for you, but the advantage is that everything is'

[04:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'perfectly placed. Again, it is flexible. So we used it around the sofa and on a few walls. This is a walnut finish, and we really liked this dark wood . Hmm, you have to'

[04:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be careful with using dark wood in a van as it can visually reduce the space, but in the end we really like the result and how much it'

[04:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'simplified our job of decorating the interior. Okay, get ready for the star of our program— our aluminum T-profile. It has a lot of names on the internet when you start looking for'

[04:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'such things. Um, aluminum T- shaped profile, I guess that\'s its official name. People also call it by its brand. It seems the original brand that released it was called 80/20. That\'s why you\'ll hear it'

[04:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'called 80/20 in many American videos. This could also apply, I think, to his profile. We used a 3030 profile. That is, 3 cm by 3 cm with these grooves inside. The advantage is that it is very'

[05:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'strong and lightweight, because in a van you don\'t see every wall of the box. When you build a box out of it , it\'s essentially a frame that you then just sheathe on one side to make it look'

[05:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'nice. This comes out to be about the same weight as plywood, but in my opinion it is stronger, a little lighter, at a similar price, and very easy to set up. So if you make the box too tall,'

[05:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can just take it all apart, trim it, and reassemble it. Whereas if you built it out of plywood, you would have to build everything from scratch. We also use it on the roof rack for the solar panel. We used'

